  "entry": "code/README.md",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Load an NPLinker result pickle whose links were already computed with the NPLinker Python API. Get an overview of gene cluster families (GCFs) and molecular families (MFs), choose a link direction (GCF→MF or MF→GCF), and filter and select GCFs or MFs. Pull up the precomputed links that were made with a chosen method (Metcalf), RAW/STANDARDISED setting and cutoff; the webapp does not compute or re-threshold scores. Then sort, filter, choose columns for and export the Candidate Links table. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
